4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,120
I want to end this, too.

5
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:09,480
But you have to remember

6
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,880
the truth yourself.

7
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:12,720
Chris!

8
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:14,520
I'm sorry!

9
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,440
[Nannichakhun House 99/260]

10
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:23,900
I think that's everything.

11
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,200
Did you forget anything?

12
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:33,680
How would I know if I forgot something?

13
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,240
Talking back, huh?

14
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:37,560
Let's go.

15
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:52,520
I grew up with just my dad.

16
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,320
His work

17
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,240
made us move around a lot.

18
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,880
My life didn't have

19
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:04,000
anything particularly

20
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:06,560
special or memorable.

21
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,740
Until...

22
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:18,600
So pretty.

23
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,480
Shouldn't this one win first place?

24
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,020
Mm...

25
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,800
Chris would be glad to hear that.

26
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:31,060
Chris is the one who made this pedestal tray.

27
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:32,720
She's in our class.

28
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:35,020
She's in the group of students
making the pedestal trays.

29
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,600
That's why you haven't met her yet.

30
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:45,600
There she is.

31
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:46,740
Chris!

32
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,480
What's up, Tangdong?

33
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,560
Who's this?

34
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,520
This is "Sun." She's the new student

35
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,960
who just arrived this morning.

36
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,040
Oh...

37
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,480
Hello,

38
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,080
I'm Sun.

39
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:13,880
Hi, I'm Chris.

40
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:19,820
Sun was just saying that

41
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,000
the pedestal tray you helped the class make

42
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,780
is so pretty

43
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,200
and totally deserves first place.

44
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:28,600
Really?

45
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,400
Thanks.

46
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:38,520
Chris!

47
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:42,920
I'll get going.
I have plans with Nadear.

48
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:50,120
That's Chris's best friend from middle school.

49
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:51,880
Oh,

50
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:54,700
are you free after school?

51
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,280
Wanna eat som tam with me?

52
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,680
Yeah, I'm free today.

53
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:01,880
Okay, I'll introduce you to our group.

54
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:13,360
Back then, I could sense

55
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,960
that there would be...

56
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:19,840
many more things I'd want to remember.

57
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,760
[Third Person]

58
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:44,090
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

59
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:49,770
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

60
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:53,400
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

61
00:03:54,050 --> 00:03:59,810
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

62
00:03:59,830 --> 00:04:09,260
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

63
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:14,720
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

64
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:19,040
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

65
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:27,970
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

66
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:36,640
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

67
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:53,920
Chris...

68
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:54,840
Chris!

69
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,400
Please be okay...

70
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:58,360
Chris.

71
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,040
Chris.

72
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:02,940
Chris...

73
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,640
Please be okay, Chris.

74
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:07,700
This way. Please wait outside for now.

75
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,760
It's okay, Nadear. It's okay...

76
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,160
You have to remember

77
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:38,160
so you won't be deceived anymore.

78
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:53,400
Chris!

79
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,320
Sun,

80
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:56,800
Chris is safe.

81
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,850
Chris... Is Chris okay?

82
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:01,900
Where is Chris?

83
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:03,880
- I... I have to...
- Hey, calm down.

84
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,000
Calm down.

85
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:07,640
The bullet missed her vital organs.
She's okay.

86
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:10,080
She's recovering now.

87
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:19,920
What about you, Sun?

88
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,700
You have a brain tumor, for crying out loud.

89
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,880
How much longer are you going to
let yourself stay like this?

90
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,680
You need to have surgery.

91
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,840
Can you stop worrying about...

92
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,760
whether you'll lose your
memories or not?

93
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,240
Chris isn't the only person in your life.

94
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:41,240
You still have me

95
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,840
and your father, too.

96
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,440
I'm sorry.

97
00:07:04,580 --> 00:07:06,800
I'll tell Chris everything.

98
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,760
No matter the outcome,

99
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,600
I'll have the surgery.

100
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:53,000
Sun...

101
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:55,760
Sun.

102
00:07:57,140 --> 00:07:58,120
Chris...

103
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,480
Nadear, where are you going?

104
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:19,780
Chris is awake.

105
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,160
I have to see her.

106
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,120
Stop this already, Nadear!

107
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:26,320
Go back and delete all the footage
from the day of the accident,

108
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:27,880
and tell the police the camera is broken.

109
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:28,920
There's no need for that.

110
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:31,320
I already told the police
it was an accidental discharge,

111
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,400
and that I didn't mean to shoot Chris.

112
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:38,000
And you think Chris and Sun
will give the same statement as you?

113
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,600
Chris...

114
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:42,280
is not yours anymore, Nadear.

115
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:44,600
Get a grip already.

116
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,600
No,

117
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,360
Chris is mine.

118
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,240
Chris is mine!

119
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,440
Stop it, Nadear!

120
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,960
Chris is mine!

121
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:04,780
Nadear.

122
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,640
How did you find out

123
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:30,080
what Nadear did to me?

124
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:32,640
I wasn't sure at first.

125
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:36,480
But then Ms. Chicha's private investigator,

126
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:39,120
whom I asked to look into Nadear,

127
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,000
sent me photos of her.

128
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:46,240
Nadear's natural hair color is
light brown.

129
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:49,160
But ever since that accident,

130
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:52,400
she's dyed her hair black,

131
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:54,800
styled it just like mine,

132
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:57,260
and has never changed it since.

133
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,720
Apart from Nan,

134
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,280
Chris and Nadear

135
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:08,240
never kept in touch
with any of their old friends.

136
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,840
Neither of them was active on social media.

137
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:17,800
We both betrayed Nadear.

138
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:21,760
We made her this way.

139
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,760
Our relationship was wrong
from the beginning.

140
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:27,720
Chris said I was the other woman,

141
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,360
but the truth is,

142
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:32,440
I was her first

143
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:34,160
and only girlfriend

144
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:37,120
before she dated Nadear.

145
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:43,520
I tried contacting my old friend

146
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,200
who could give me an answer.

147
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,080
Do you have Nut's number?

148
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:51,400
I want to ask him something.

149
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,600
There are many possible causes of memory loss,

150
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,400
from accidents and psychological trauma

151
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:57,740
to the brain tumor you have.

152
00:10:58,260 --> 00:10:59,720
What about misremembering,

153
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,720
mixing up memories,

154
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,120
or having false memories?

155
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,380
People usually call this déjà vu.

156
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:10,160
You feel like you've experienced
something before, even though you haven't.

157
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:12,220
The opposite is called jamais vu.

158
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,460
You know you've seen something before,

159
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,880
but somehow you don't recognize it.

160
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:17,680
Can hypnosis make you

161
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:19,760
misremember things

162
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,800
or remember things that never happened?

163
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,600
I don't want to say this, because...

164
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:31,600
it's not something you should do.

165
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:33,560
As a doctor, you should know that

166
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:36,260
anything that's not
medical treatment is a violation.

167
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,640
It's a crime.

168
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:41,960
I didn't do it.

169
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:44,080
I just want to save someone I love.

170
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:47,160
What should I do, then?

171
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:49,600
Listen,

172
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:53,240
our brains don't store memories
like a video recording.

173
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,040
Instead, our memories are

174
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:57,160
stored in small fragments.

175
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:59,540
When we think of something
related to that memory,

176
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,780
our minds

177
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:03,480
slowly piece together fragments of

178
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:04,720
what we can remember.

179
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:06,560
But as we piece them together,

180
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:08,340
they can become distorted

181
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:10,880
by interference, such as hypnosis.

182
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,200
How do I fix that?

183
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:17,200
Hey, Sun, we're living in the 21st century.

184
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:20,000
Sure, our memories aren't
recorded like videos.

185
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,960
But we do have cameras.

186
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,060
Photos, videos, and notes.

187
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,400
There are tons of things like that.

188
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,840
I don't know if the person you love

189
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:30,060
will get their memories back.

190
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:31,200
But one thing's for sure,

191
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:33,040
they'll know what's true and what isn't.

192
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:40,620
Like I've said before.

193
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:44,160
I couldn't remember anything then.

194
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:47,480
But after I met Tangdong,

195
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:51,560
I was able to piece my
fragmented memories back together.

196
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:55,600
But in your case,

197
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:59,200
I'm not expecting you to remember right away.

198
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:03,120
I just don't want you to be deceived anymore.

199
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:18,240
How much do you remember?

200
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:23,680
I'm not sure.

201
00:13:27,620 --> 00:13:29,100
I only know...

202
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:31,480
my memories have changed.

203
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:34,360
Because, in reality,

204
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:38,240
everything I remembered about Nadear

205
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:40,720
was actually you.

206
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,480
It was you all along.

207
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:53,080
I could feel your eyes

208
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:55,920
always watching me.

209
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:58,040
Is someone looking at me?

210
00:13:58,560 --> 00:13:59,320
Yeah.

211
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:00,920
She didn't even look away.

212
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,800
Ugh, what the heck is wrong with her?

213
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,300
She is

214
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,500
the new kid

215
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,680
we asked to join our group yesterday.

216
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:10,480
Huh?

217
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:11,860
Mm.

218
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:14,640
Tangdong said she's pretty sweet.

219
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,400
Why don't you give her a chance?

220
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:44,920
Chris!

221
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:01,000
You!

222
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,280
Run three laps around the field!

223
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:16,240
Hey!

224
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:17,400
Be more careful.

225
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,920
Do you want to get caught
buying stuff from outside the school?

226
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,360
Hey, you two!

227
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:27,520
What are you doing?!

228
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,280
Run!

229
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:33,760
Get up there!

230
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,320
Get down, get down.

231
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,560
Why did we have to run this far?

232
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,360
Well, I was scared.

233
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,520
Do you think...

234
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,320
he'll find us here?

235
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:00,600
Maybe he will

236
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:02,760
if you keep letting the smell of meatballs
waft around like this.

237
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,520
This is my first time skipping class.

238
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,500
If you weren't waiting for
your food out in the open like that,

239
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,960
would our first time be like this?

240
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:25,440
We had to run for our lives, you see?

241
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:30,120
That was fun.

242
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:31,840
Huh?

243
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:35,760
I said,

244
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:38,720
skipping class with you today was fun.

245
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:57,880
Kiiro is hungry.

246
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:01,680
Kiiro...

247
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:02,840
Come on.

248
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:06,080
Go.

249
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:08,060
Time to eat.

250
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:08,800
Let's go.

251
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:15,080
Are you having a sleepover
with your friends?

252
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:16,940
Mm.

253
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,400
That way, I'll get to leave my room.

254
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:22,360
Tell your friends that you want to
spend some time with your girlfriend.

255
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:25,560
They'll think I'm avoiding them.

256
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:27,300
You worry about what your friends think,

257
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:28,920
but you don't worry
if your girlfriend misses you?

258
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,360
I'm not worried.

259
00:17:33,250 --> 00:17:34,880
Because I'll make sure you never have to miss me.

260
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:55,120
I missed you...

261
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:58,640
I missed you so much...

262
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,100
I'm sorry.

263
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:18,440
I'm so sorry for making you miss me.

264
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:30,120
I'm the one who should apologize.

265
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:34,440
I was the one who left you.

266
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,680
Was it because you lost your memories?

267
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,400
I didn't lose my memories
because of the accident.

268
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:45,440
I lost my memories because...

269
00:18:47,740 --> 00:18:50,200
I have a tumor near my brainstem.

270
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:57,400
That accident

271
00:18:58,440 --> 00:19:00,600
made me realize I have a tumor.

272
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:05,460
I might die or lose my memories.

273
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:10,680
I knew you'd just lost your parents.

274
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:15,240
I didn't want you to go
through all that again.

275
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,480
It's a good thing you forgot.

276
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,760
It's a good thing you had Nadear.

277
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:31,040
Although my brain forgot,

278
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:35,680
my heart never forgot you.

279
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:44,320
I only realized

280
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,240
when I moved overseas
with my father for treatment

281
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:52,160
that I was still alive.

282
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,840
I lost my memories,

283
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:00,720
but some feelings remained.

284
00:20:02,620 --> 00:20:04,040
Someone

285
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:08,000
who stayed in my heart.

286
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:12,080
Someone I never forgot.

287
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:21,960
Why do you want to come here?

288
00:20:22,780 --> 00:20:23,840
You know this place?

289
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,840
Or did you get your memories back?

290
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:28,360
No,

291
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,400
not yet.

292
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,600
But I really want to remember.

293
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:47,560
Sun?

294
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:49,840
Do you know me?

295
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,520
Of course I do.

296
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:55,560
She...

297
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,040
seems to know you.

298
00:21:02,180 --> 00:21:04,560
Oh, sorry. It took me forever to find this.

299
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:05,560
Here.

300
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:08,000
It's alright. The food here is amazing.

301
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:09,160
Really?

302
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,400
Thanks.

303
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:18,000
So pretty...

304
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,000
What?

305
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:20,120
This one.

306
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:22,360
The lotus flowers are folded

307
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,900
and intricately arranged

308
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,280
on this pedestal tray.

309
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:32,720
What's wrong?

310
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:35,540
Oh, Sun,

311
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:38,120
you're still the same
even without your memories.

312
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:45,720
You fell in love with the same person.

313
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:50,500
Here.

314
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:52,300
The one who folded the lotus petals,

315
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,880
and the one you fell for.

316
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:23,640
Chris...

317
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,720
Thank you for remembering.

318
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:06,720
Thank you for making me remember.

319
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,400
Did you know?

320
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:23,800
I was going to let you go.

321
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:27,920
But when I touched you again,

322
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:30,960
I realized...

323
00:23:32,140 --> 00:23:34,520
that I can't let you go.

324
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:38,320
I couldn't come back

325
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:41,560
as the Sun you used to know

326
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:45,880
because I felt guilty.

327
00:23:48,020 --> 00:23:50,120
That's why I wanted to give us a fresh start.

328
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:53,040
Then I found out

329
00:23:53,460 --> 00:23:55,200
you'd been hypnotized

330
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,240
and your memories were all mixed up.

331
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:02,120
That's why I had to find a way

332
00:24:02,260 --> 00:24:04,000
to help you remember,

333
00:24:05,160 --> 00:24:07,160
even though I was scared

334
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:10,700
that you wouldn't forgive me.

335
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:16,560
Did you know?

336
00:24:18,760 --> 00:24:21,160
I never went all the way with Nadear.

337
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:25,180
Because every time I was about to,

338
00:24:26,120 --> 00:24:28,320
my body would reject it.

339
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:30,060
At first, I thought

340
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:32,520
it was because I was traumatized
by that accident.

341
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:36,760
But now that I know the truth,

342
00:24:37,780 --> 00:24:39,320
I finally understand...

343
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:43,400
it was because I never forgot you.

344
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,320
Thank you

345
00:24:47,580 --> 00:24:49,060
for never forgetting me.

346
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:56,360
I feel even more guilty hearing that,

347
00:24:59,860 --> 00:25:01,860
but it makes me love you even more, too.

348
00:25:09,260 --> 00:25:11,240
Stop blaming yourself.

349
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:14,320
It was my fault.

350
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:18,180
If I'd been stronger back then,

351
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:22,060
both you and Nadear

352
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:24,240
wouldn't have had to do all this for me.

353
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:27,800
If I hadn't been so weak,

354
00:25:28,680 --> 00:25:31,020
things wouldn't have turned out this way.

355
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,240
Can you stay strong for me?

356
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,880
I'll stay strong for you.

357
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:44,880
I just found out

358
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:52,080
that the tumor near my brainstem is back.

359
00:25:56,840 --> 00:25:58,380
I might forget everything about you again.

360
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:05,040
♫That you'd be something I made up♫

361
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:11,680
♫I'm so confused♫

362
00:26:12,220 --> 00:26:19,100
♫Who am I waiting for?♫

363
00:26:19,120 --> 00:26:22,980
♫Trapped in a love that's a fading image,♫

364
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,900
[Third Person]

365
00:26:26,784 --> 00:26:29,264
[Third Person]

366
00:26:29,284 --> 00:26:32,304
You don't have to worry about
losing your memories,

367
00:26:32,704 --> 00:26:34,464
since you have her by your side.

368
00:26:34,584 --> 00:26:35,264
Hm?

369
00:26:35,764 --> 00:26:36,424
Right?

370
00:26:36,564 --> 00:26:37,784
Yes, Dad.

371
00:26:38,524 --> 00:26:40,504
But if she loses her memories again,

372
00:26:40,524 --> 00:26:42,224
- please count me out.
- Oh?

373
00:26:43,144 --> 00:26:44,124
It's quite exhausting.

374
00:26:44,144 --> 00:26:45,784
Why?

375
00:26:46,664 --> 00:26:47,864
It's alright.

376
00:26:48,004 --> 00:26:49,704
If she loses her memories,

377
00:26:50,264 --> 00:26:51,424
I'll help her this time.

378
00:26:55,824 --> 00:26:56,584
Sweet.

379
00:27:01,204 --> 00:27:01,944
Oh,

380
00:27:02,724 --> 00:27:03,504
and...

381
00:27:03,964 --> 00:27:05,464
what about the case?

382
00:27:08,104 --> 00:27:09,924
Are you ready to give
your statements to the police?

383
00:27:13,544 --> 00:27:14,664
Actually...

384
00:27:15,224 --> 00:27:16,744
Dr. Jeen wants to talk to us.

385
00:27:17,744 --> 00:27:18,784
What do you think?

386
00:27:19,504 --> 00:27:20,384
Let's go.

387
00:27:21,244 --> 00:27:23,584
I want to meet that
unethical doctor myself.

388
00:27:24,744 --> 00:27:26,544
I want to know what she has to say.

389
00:27:29,144 --> 00:27:31,304
I told Nadear to tell the police

390
00:27:32,584 --> 00:27:33,984
it was an accident,

391
00:27:35,344 --> 00:27:36,784
that she had accidentally fired the gun.

392
00:27:37,544 --> 00:27:39,784
Even though you knew what really happened.

393
00:27:40,144 --> 00:27:41,224
But it's true

394
00:27:41,444 --> 00:27:42,864
Nadear wasn't thinking clearly.

395
00:27:43,864 --> 00:27:45,624
And she loves you very much, Chris.

396
00:27:47,304 --> 00:27:50,224
When she learned from her senior
that you were safe,

397
00:27:50,864 --> 00:27:52,224
she went into a frenzy

398
00:27:52,484 --> 00:27:53,984
and insisted on seeing you.

399
00:27:54,844 --> 00:27:56,424
I had to give her sedatives

400
00:27:56,444 --> 00:27:57,704
to calm her down.

401
00:28:00,464 --> 00:28:01,424
Then what?

402
00:28:02,704 --> 00:28:03,584
Chris,

403
00:28:04,844 --> 00:28:06,304
you do know how much

404
00:28:06,324 --> 00:28:08,104
Nadear has done for you, right?

405
00:28:09,104 --> 00:28:10,784
Ever since that accident,

406
00:28:11,284 --> 00:28:12,924
you've only had Nadear, haven't you?

407
00:28:20,864 --> 00:28:22,204
No one

408
00:28:22,944 --> 00:28:24,424
loves you more than Nadear does.

409
00:28:24,604 --> 00:28:25,504
No!

410
00:28:26,864 --> 00:28:28,304
How would you even measure that?

411
00:28:28,904 --> 00:28:30,984
Nadear doesn't even have the right
to love Chris,

412
00:28:32,144 --> 00:28:33,904
because Chris's true love

413
00:28:34,504 --> 00:28:35,464
is me.

414
00:28:35,984 --> 00:28:36,904
The lover

415
00:28:37,744 --> 00:28:39,344
who left Chris

416
00:28:40,144 --> 00:28:42,184
when she lost her memory, huh?

417
00:28:42,784 --> 00:28:44,224
I didn't want to leave her,

418
00:28:45,864 --> 00:28:47,224
but I had to

419
00:28:48,544 --> 00:28:50,544
because I had a tumor near my brainstem,

420
00:28:52,584 --> 00:28:53,584
and I could die

421
00:28:53,604 --> 00:28:55,504
or lose my memories of her forever.

422
00:28:57,664 --> 00:28:59,344
If there was one thing I was wrong about,

423
00:28:59,824 --> 00:29:01,824
it was thinking...

424
00:29:02,344 --> 00:29:04,664
Nadear would actually take care of Chris,

425
00:29:05,824 --> 00:29:07,184
instead of brainwashing her.

426
00:29:08,704 --> 00:29:10,584
I really can't believe

427
00:29:11,384 --> 00:29:13,344
a doctor as unethical as you

428
00:29:13,664 --> 00:29:15,864
would not only refuse to
treat your patient,

429
00:29:16,224 --> 00:29:18,984
but also implant false memories
in her mind.

430
00:29:19,504 --> 00:29:20,424
Is that so?

431
00:29:22,144 --> 00:29:23,704
You think that because you might die

432
00:29:24,004 --> 00:29:25,424
or lose your memory,

433
00:29:25,804 --> 00:29:29,044
you had the right to make
someone else's life a living hell?

434
00:29:33,184 --> 00:29:34,264
Isn't it ironic?

435
00:29:34,724 --> 00:29:38,024
The one who caused
all of this in the first place

436
00:29:38,824 --> 00:29:40,864
is now lecturing

437
00:29:41,664 --> 00:29:43,464
about who's right and who's wrong.

438
00:29:44,544 --> 00:29:46,024
When in fact,

439
00:29:47,004 --> 00:29:48,404
the first person at fault

440
00:29:51,144 --> 00:29:52,424
was you, of all people.

441
00:29:53,964 --> 00:29:55,144
What are you trying to say?

442
00:29:55,704 --> 00:29:58,704
Nobody wants to be someone else.

443
00:29:59,344 --> 00:30:01,224
Nadear didn't want to be Sun

444
00:30:01,244 --> 00:30:02,544
to make you love her,

445
00:30:04,664 --> 00:30:06,264
but she wanted to be Sun

446
00:30:07,504 --> 00:30:09,184
to save your life.

447
00:30:15,784 --> 00:30:16,784
Chris...

448
00:30:17,544 --> 00:30:18,664
wake up.

449
00:30:19,944 --> 00:30:23,024
I brought my senior, who's
a psychiatrist, to help you.

450
00:30:31,864 --> 00:30:32,664
Chris.

451
00:30:41,064 --> 00:30:41,784
Nadear,

452
00:30:42,784 --> 00:30:43,944
call an ambulance!

453
00:30:46,184 --> 00:30:47,524
What?

454
00:30:47,544 --> 00:30:48,904
Call an ambulance!

455
00:30:49,364 --> 00:30:50,464
Hurry, Nadear!

456
00:30:52,484 --> 00:30:53,684
What happened?!

457
00:30:53,704 --> 00:30:55,024
I'll call an ambulance.

458
00:30:56,064 --> 00:30:56,904
Chris!

459
00:30:57,684 --> 00:30:59,024
You tried to kill yourself.

460
00:30:59,744 --> 00:31:01,744
Although I saved your life,

461
00:31:04,784 --> 00:31:06,484
Nadear was in a living hell.

462
00:31:07,544 --> 00:31:09,224
Chris is going to die because of her.

463
00:31:10,864 --> 00:31:12,464
But if she dies,

464
00:31:13,184 --> 00:31:14,584
I won't be able to go on living.

465
00:31:20,224 --> 00:31:21,304
Who, Nadear?

466
00:31:22,964 --> 00:31:24,664
The woman who left Chris.

467
00:31:27,104 --> 00:31:28,864
Why couldn't it be me?

468
00:31:29,424 --> 00:31:31,424
I'd never make Chris suffer.

469
00:31:33,304 --> 00:31:34,504
Jeen...

470
00:31:36,484 --> 00:31:39,304
can you make me that woman?

471
00:31:43,144 --> 00:31:44,384
I can't do that.

472
00:31:44,824 --> 00:31:47,344
So you'll let Chris die,

473
00:31:48,944 --> 00:31:50,864
and you'll let me die, too, right?

474
00:31:51,504 --> 00:31:53,504
Nadear knew what I was capable of,

475
00:31:53,624 --> 00:31:55,144
so she asked me to do that.

476
00:31:56,104 --> 00:31:57,584
In the end...

477
00:31:58,084 --> 00:31:59,184
I caved in

478
00:32:00,264 --> 00:32:01,944
because I didn't want anyone to die.

479
00:32:03,424 --> 00:32:06,304
My lover is Nadear.

480
00:32:09,344 --> 00:32:11,144
I first met her

481
00:32:11,624 --> 00:32:13,184
back in high school.

482
00:32:16,864 --> 00:32:19,544
She transferred to my school
in eleventh grade.

483
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:23,064
She has fair skin,

484
00:32:25,344 --> 00:32:26,504
a small frame,

485
00:32:28,784 --> 00:32:30,384
jet-black hair,

486
00:32:32,964 --> 00:32:34,784
and a bright smile.

487
00:32:36,424 --> 00:32:38,664
This smell always

488
00:32:40,024 --> 00:32:42,504
reminds me of...

489
00:32:44,064 --> 00:32:46,064
Nadear,

490
00:32:48,024 --> 00:32:49,384
my lover.

491
00:32:53,024 --> 00:32:55,024
Nadear changed herself to look like Sun.

492
00:32:57,024 --> 00:32:58,964
And I thought that

493
00:32:58,984 --> 00:33:01,064
Nadear was my lover.

494
00:33:02,264 --> 00:33:03,944
But you never loved Nadear.

495
00:33:08,504 --> 00:33:10,264
Even though Nadear
changed herself to look like Sun,

496
00:33:13,424 --> 00:33:15,224
you always rejected her.

497
00:33:17,464 --> 00:33:19,824
When you said I rejected physical contact,

498
00:33:20,064 --> 00:33:21,384
was it because of the accident?

499
00:33:22,184 --> 00:33:24,024
Your subconscious mind

500
00:33:25,284 --> 00:33:27,864
was rejecting intimacy with other women.

501
00:33:28,904 --> 00:33:30,024
That was why

502
00:33:31,004 --> 00:33:33,584
I told you to be open-minded.

503
00:33:34,344 --> 00:33:35,664
Because I thought

504
00:33:35,804 --> 00:33:37,144
if you fell for someone else,

505
00:33:37,544 --> 00:33:39,144
Nadear might be able to move on.

506
00:33:41,744 --> 00:33:43,184
But that wasn't the case.

507
00:33:45,564 --> 00:33:46,784
I'll do it for you, Nadear.

508
00:33:48,104 --> 00:33:50,224
Nadear, Nadear... Nadear!

509
00:33:50,644 --> 00:33:52,104
I had to hypnotize you

510
00:33:53,784 --> 00:33:55,584
to create a new memory

511
00:33:57,824 --> 00:33:59,904
that you had an affair with Sun

512
00:34:01,504 --> 00:34:03,004
to make you feel guilty,

513
00:34:03,864 --> 00:34:05,224
so you'd stay by Nadear's side.

514
00:34:06,664 --> 00:34:08,264
And how does that help Chris?

515
00:34:11,344 --> 00:34:13,384
This was just a selfish act
that you and Nadear

516
00:34:13,404 --> 00:34:14,864
conspired to carry out.

517
00:34:19,084 --> 00:34:19,864
Yes,

518
00:34:21,324 --> 00:34:22,704
I know

519
00:34:23,024 --> 00:34:25,024
that we were just lying to ourselves.

520
00:34:27,044 --> 00:34:29,544
Whether you lost your memories or not,

521
00:34:30,304 --> 00:34:31,904
you don't have feelings for Nadear.

522
00:34:33,644 --> 00:34:35,744
And if those false memories

523
00:34:35,864 --> 00:34:38,264
are replaced by the truth one day,

524
00:34:40,064 --> 00:34:41,464
Nadear will be the one

525
00:34:42,094 --> 00:34:43,904
who suffers all over again.

526
00:34:46,884 --> 00:34:48,264
What do you want, then?

527
00:34:51,144 --> 00:34:52,704
Nadear has psychological issues.

528
00:34:53,544 --> 00:34:55,624
She's practically dying inside already.

529
00:34:57,944 --> 00:34:59,464
Can you...

530
00:35:01,504 --> 00:35:03,144
tell the police

531
00:35:05,384 --> 00:35:07,224
that Chris was shot

532
00:35:08,084 --> 00:35:09,784
because the gun went off by accident?

533
00:35:11,024 --> 00:35:12,784
I'll treat Nadear myself.

534
00:35:13,524 --> 00:35:15,524
She won't bother you both again.

535
00:35:20,144 --> 00:35:21,224
As for...

536
00:35:22,504 --> 00:35:24,504
the fact that I hypnotized you,

537
00:35:25,824 --> 00:35:27,344
you can report it to the police

538
00:35:29,524 --> 00:35:31,024
or do whatever you want.

539
00:35:47,064 --> 00:35:49,184
Aren't we done with all this lying already?

540
00:36:00,584 --> 00:36:02,224
Don't worry too much.

541
00:36:03,224 --> 00:36:05,304
You're having surgery
in just a couple of days,

542
00:36:05,944 --> 00:36:07,744
so focus on getting better first.

543
00:36:16,064 --> 00:36:16,904
Chris,

544
00:36:19,224 --> 00:36:20,824
I want to talk to Nadear.

545
00:36:36,904 --> 00:36:38,424
Take some medicine, Nadear.

546
00:36:39,384 --> 00:36:42,424
Uncle and Auntie will pick you up
so you can live with them today.

547
00:36:43,304 --> 00:36:44,744
Why?

548
00:36:46,204 --> 00:36:48,664
I'm going to jail anyway.

549
00:36:49,364 --> 00:36:50,904
Don't say that.

550
00:36:51,544 --> 00:36:54,224
I won't let you go to jail.

551
00:36:54,944 --> 00:36:56,944
Even if Chris and Sun don't help,

552
00:36:57,744 --> 00:36:59,344
I'll help you myself.

553
00:37:11,004 --> 00:37:13,064
Can you guess who's waiting at the door?

554
00:37:13,904 --> 00:37:15,624
Is it my dad,

555
00:37:16,224 --> 00:37:17,064
my mom,

556
00:37:18,784 --> 00:37:20,024
or the police?

557
00:37:40,744 --> 00:37:42,104
I'll wait outside.

558
00:38:00,444 --> 00:38:02,444
I heard you're having brain surgery.

559
00:38:04,644 --> 00:38:05,864
Still alive, huh?

560
00:38:14,404 --> 00:38:16,964
[Third Person]

561
00:38:18,764 --> 00:38:20,964
[Third Person]

562
00:38:27,364 --> 00:38:28,204
Kiiro.

563
00:38:33,084 --> 00:38:35,164
I once named a fish "Kiiro."

564
00:38:35,524 --> 00:38:36,984
But it died,

565
00:38:37,644 --> 00:38:39,564
so Nadear got me a replacement.

566
00:38:40,724 --> 00:38:42,724
You said it couldn't be replaced.

567
00:38:44,604 --> 00:38:45,604
Yeah.

568
00:38:46,724 --> 00:38:48,724
But I can't take care of it either.

569
00:38:50,484 --> 00:38:51,844
I don't even

570
00:38:52,804 --> 00:38:54,364
want to call it by its name.

571
00:38:57,284 --> 00:38:59,124
Dr. Jeen said you're sick.

572
00:39:00,324 --> 00:39:04,204
Someone who's been betrayed
over and over again like me

573
00:39:05,524 --> 00:39:08,004
should have died a long time ago.

574
00:39:09,564 --> 00:39:11,524
No one betrayed you, Nadear.

575
00:39:13,044 --> 00:39:15,404
Back then, Sun left me
because she was sick.

576
00:39:16,764 --> 00:39:19,484
I appreciate that you wanted to help me,

577
00:39:20,484 --> 00:39:23,004
but you shouldn't deceive me like this.

578
00:39:23,844 --> 00:39:25,844
So I should just let you die, then?

579
00:39:31,224 --> 00:39:32,304
You're sick again.

580
00:39:33,724 --> 00:39:35,344
It's happening again, isn't it?

581
00:39:36,464 --> 00:39:38,844
Why didn't you leave Chris this time?

582
00:39:39,644 --> 00:39:40,924
I'm sorry.

583
00:39:41,704 --> 00:39:42,874
Don't apologize to me.

584
00:39:43,244 --> 00:39:45,144
The more you apologize,

585
00:39:45,164 --> 00:39:48,324
the more I feel like
I'm being forced to forgive you.

586
00:39:49,384 --> 00:39:51,284
But if I forgive you,

587
00:39:51,844 --> 00:39:53,404
you'll feel relieved.

588
00:39:54,184 --> 00:39:56,564
Why does it have to be you

589
00:39:56,844 --> 00:39:59,364
who gets forgiven and
gets to be with Chris?

590
00:40:05,404 --> 00:40:06,244
Nadear,

591
00:40:06,884 --> 00:40:07,544
I'm sorry.

592
00:40:07,564 --> 00:40:09,844
Stop apologizing to me!

593
00:40:12,364 --> 00:40:13,884
You didn't do anything wrong,

594
00:40:13,904 --> 00:40:16,044
so why are you apologizing to me?!

595
00:40:16,764 --> 00:40:18,404
Are you trying to force me

596
00:40:19,744 --> 00:40:22,124
to let go of you and Sun?

597
00:40:28,244 --> 00:40:30,084
I've already done that.

598
00:40:32,484 --> 00:40:34,324
I've let you go before,

599
00:40:36,784 --> 00:40:40,364
even though I loved you first.

600
00:40:43,524 --> 00:40:45,724
My parents are dead.

601
00:40:48,084 --> 00:40:48,964
Nadear.

602
00:40:52,204 --> 00:40:53,484
It's okay.

603
00:40:54,724 --> 00:40:56,324
You still have me.

604
00:40:58,224 --> 00:41:00,324
I'll stay by your side.

605
00:41:04,324 --> 00:41:05,164
You.

606
00:41:05,684 --> 00:41:06,404
Oh.

607
00:41:06,424 --> 00:41:07,404
Hello, Nadear.

608
00:41:09,204 --> 00:41:10,644
Thanks for coming.

609
00:41:13,824 --> 00:41:14,884
See?

610
00:41:15,444 --> 00:41:16,684
Nadear came to see you, too.

611
00:41:17,724 --> 00:41:19,324
You still have me

612
00:41:19,524 --> 00:41:20,644
and Nadear.

613
00:41:22,084 --> 00:41:23,884
Everything's gonna be alright.

614
00:41:30,004 --> 00:41:31,404
I loved you so much

615
00:41:32,034 --> 00:41:34,164
that I let Sun move in with us

616
00:41:34,824 --> 00:41:37,204
so I could take care of you.

617
00:41:39,644 --> 00:41:42,204
But I was the other woman all this time.

618
00:41:47,484 --> 00:41:48,604
Kiiro,

619
00:41:49,324 --> 00:41:50,844
it's time to eat.

620
00:42:00,364 --> 00:42:01,564
Kiiro!

621
00:42:02,804 --> 00:42:04,524
Kiiro...

622
00:42:08,064 --> 00:42:09,924
Someone opened the door.

623
00:42:14,884 --> 00:42:16,004
I'm sorry.

624
00:42:17,164 --> 00:42:19,344
It's my fault for not
taking better care of him.

625
00:42:20,024 --> 00:42:22,124
You're not the one who should apologize.

626
00:42:32,184 --> 00:42:33,764
Are you sure you didn't forget anything?

627
00:42:34,924 --> 00:42:35,964
What about you?

628
00:42:36,164 --> 00:42:37,524
Are you sure

629
00:42:38,084 --> 00:42:39,484
you're moving out?

630
00:42:44,084 --> 00:42:46,324
I'll go wherever you go.

631
00:42:47,404 --> 00:42:48,664
And I know

632
00:42:48,684 --> 00:42:50,324
you might not feel comfortable

633
00:42:50,384 --> 00:42:51,784
if I stayed here with Nadear.

634
00:42:56,804 --> 00:42:57,604
Chris,

635
00:42:59,364 --> 00:43:01,364
I don't want to be someone

636
00:43:01,884 --> 00:43:03,964
who comes between you and your friend.

637
00:43:05,884 --> 00:43:07,884
I don't want to stay here

638
00:43:08,844 --> 00:43:10,164
because I'm sure

639
00:43:12,304 --> 00:43:13,684
Nadear has feelings for you.

640
00:43:23,204 --> 00:43:24,924
And I'm not sure

641
00:43:26,324 --> 00:43:28,124
if Kiiro

642
00:43:30,884 --> 00:43:32,244
was killed.

643
00:43:34,904 --> 00:43:36,644
Sun, it's not that I don't believe you,

644
00:43:38,644 --> 00:43:40,524
but Nadear is my best friend.

645
00:43:43,564 --> 00:43:45,724
We could never be separated.

646
00:43:50,924 --> 00:43:52,484
But when it comes to love,

647
00:43:54,304 --> 00:43:55,984
you're the only one for me.

648
00:43:59,124 --> 00:44:00,204
So,

649
00:44:00,604 --> 00:44:02,604
wherever you go, I'll go with you.

650
00:44:04,324 --> 00:44:05,844
I believe Nadear will understand.

651
00:44:09,964 --> 00:44:11,164
Then tomorrow,

652
00:44:11,704 --> 00:44:13,844
let's tell Nadear we're moving out.

653
00:44:18,884 --> 00:44:20,564
Chris is going to leave.

654
00:44:21,644 --> 00:44:23,204
Tomorrow,

655
00:44:23,344 --> 00:44:25,344
she won't be here anymore.

656
00:44:26,524 --> 00:44:28,644
I just kept driving

657
00:44:29,324 --> 00:44:30,804
with no destination in mind.

658
00:44:31,664 --> 00:44:33,204
Before I knew it,

659
00:44:33,964 --> 00:44:35,524
I was at a dead end.

660
00:44:39,724 --> 00:44:41,844
[Chris]

661
00:44:46,524 --> 00:44:47,444
Chris.

662
00:44:47,804 --> 00:44:49,124
Nadear, where are you?

663
00:44:49,764 --> 00:44:51,484
I don't know either.

664
00:44:52,284 --> 00:44:53,764
Nadear, calm down.

665
00:44:53,964 --> 00:44:55,964
Can you send me your location?

666
00:44:58,284 --> 00:44:59,584
Are you coming to see me?

667
00:44:59,604 --> 00:45:00,624
Yeah,

668
00:45:00,644 --> 00:45:02,044
I'll come to you.

669
00:45:02,404 --> 00:45:04,964
I went to look for you with Chris

670
00:45:06,224 --> 00:45:07,984
because she was very worried about you.

671
00:45:10,484 --> 00:45:11,384
I waited?

672
00:45:11,404 --> 00:45:12,024
[Chris, calling...]

673
00:45:12,044 --> 00:45:14,124
because Chris had never broken a promise to me.

674
00:45:15,444 --> 00:45:17,204
But it was taking too long.

675
00:45:30,004 --> 00:45:32,124
Thanks for coming with me, Sun.

676
00:45:34,124 --> 00:45:35,604
I already told you

677
00:45:36,044 --> 00:45:37,524
I understand

678
00:45:38,104 --> 00:45:40,444
that Nadear is

679
00:45:41,924 --> 00:45:43,204
a very dear friend to you.

680
00:45:46,204 --> 00:45:47,124
But...

681
00:45:47,844 --> 00:45:49,204
what's wrong with Nadear?

682
00:45:49,764 --> 00:45:51,964
I think her parents pressured her.

683
00:45:52,844 --> 00:45:54,324
Nadear tends to be like this.

684
00:45:54,644 --> 00:45:56,444
She always keeps her worries to herself

685
00:45:57,084 --> 00:45:59,284
and sneaks off to cry alone.

686
00:46:03,364 --> 00:46:05,324
But you knew that about her.

687
00:46:07,564 --> 00:46:08,724
At least,

688
00:46:09,364 --> 00:46:10,684
Nadear has you, Chris.

689
00:46:19,604 --> 00:46:21,164
Thanks again, Sun.

690
00:46:30,584 --> 00:46:31,644
Whoa!

691
00:46:44,504 --> 00:46:45,244
Chris!

692
00:46:45,544 --> 00:46:46,324
Chris!

693
00:46:47,084 --> 00:46:47,844
Chris!

694
00:46:48,364 --> 00:46:49,164
Chris!

695
00:46:49,564 --> 00:46:50,324
Chris!

696
00:46:50,844 --> 00:46:51,684
Please...

697
00:46:51,904 --> 00:46:53,284
Please help Sun.

698
00:47:03,844 --> 00:47:05,644
Back then, I blamed myself.

699
00:47:08,404 --> 00:47:10,044
All I could do was pray

700
00:47:10,684 --> 00:47:13,724
that you two would be safe.

701
00:47:15,284 --> 00:47:16,484
And this time,

702
00:47:18,644 --> 00:47:21,564
I was willing to be friends
with both of you.

703
00:47:22,164 --> 00:47:23,124
But then...

704
00:47:23,984 --> 00:47:25,364
I disappeared.

705
00:47:26,504 --> 00:47:27,404
That's right.

706
00:47:28,564 --> 00:47:31,244
Sa-run told me you ran away abroad

707
00:47:31,964 --> 00:47:34,044
and left Chris behind
when she lost her memory.

708
00:47:38,324 --> 00:47:40,404
I was the one who told him

709
00:47:41,104 --> 00:47:42,444
to keep it a secret,

710
00:47:44,764 --> 00:47:46,424
because I might die.

711
00:47:48,324 --> 00:47:50,484
I didn't want anyone to pity me,

712
00:47:53,924 --> 00:47:55,244
and I didn't know

713
00:47:56,844 --> 00:47:58,724
Chris was affected this badly.

714
00:48:04,304 --> 00:48:07,804
Chris had already lost
her parents in an accident once.

715
00:48:09,244 --> 00:48:12,364
Losing someone again
in a similar incident

716
00:48:13,044 --> 00:48:14,604
hurt her deeply.

717
00:48:15,044 --> 00:48:16,684
But you still did it.

718
00:48:22,224 --> 00:48:24,084
We were all in the wrong.

719
00:48:25,884 --> 00:48:28,844
Had I cared about you more...

720
00:48:33,084 --> 00:48:35,124
Had I listened to what Sun said...

721
00:48:38,324 --> 00:48:41,384
Had I gone to therapy
after losing my parents

722
00:48:41,404 --> 00:48:43,164
and become stronger...

723
00:48:44,604 --> 00:48:46,404
Had I been stronger,

724
00:48:47,684 --> 00:48:50,884
you and Sun wouldn't
have had to do all of this for me.

725
00:49:01,044 --> 00:49:02,204
I get it now.

726
00:49:06,884 --> 00:49:09,604
I finally know who's to blame.

727
00:49:12,024 --> 00:49:14,124
What you just said

728
00:49:15,884 --> 00:49:17,924
has really opened my eyes.

729
00:49:19,924 --> 00:49:21,064
Now I know

730
00:49:21,524 --> 00:49:23,004
I fell in love with the wrong person.

731
00:49:25,604 --> 00:49:27,804
I should never have fallen
for someone like you.

732
00:49:34,204 --> 00:49:35,604
But luckily,

733
00:49:36,024 --> 00:49:38,024
I've already gotten back at you.

734
00:49:44,404 --> 00:49:46,044
I slept with Jeen

735
00:49:48,964 --> 00:49:50,964
in exchange for her hypnotizing you

736
00:49:51,644 --> 00:49:54,004
into distorting your memories.

737
00:49:55,004 --> 00:49:55,844
How was that?

738
00:49:57,404 --> 00:49:58,924
It hurts, doesn't it?

739
00:50:01,124 --> 00:50:02,084
Nadear.

740
00:50:13,004 --> 00:50:14,204
As for you,

741
00:50:16,804 --> 00:50:18,044
congratulations.

742
00:50:19,724 --> 00:50:21,484
In the end,

743
00:50:22,364 --> 00:50:25,764
you ended up with someone
who's both weak and cowardly.

744
00:50:28,244 --> 00:50:30,364
I'm finally free from all of this.

745
00:50:45,984 --> 00:50:48,044
Just tell the police
what really happened.

746
00:50:49,364 --> 00:50:51,844
I don't want pity from either of you.

747
00:51:23,724 --> 00:51:25,924
[Third Person]

748
00:51:27,942 --> 00:51:29,942
[Third Person]

749
00:51:41,762 --> 00:51:44,262
You're about to have surgery.
Take care of yourself, will you?

750
00:51:45,202 --> 00:51:46,502
You're the one

751
00:51:46,902 --> 00:51:48,502
who needs to take care of yourself

752
00:51:49,702 --> 00:51:51,922
so I can go into surgery
with peace of mind.

753
00:51:53,762 --> 00:51:55,542
What are you thinking about out here?

754
00:52:01,062 --> 00:52:02,662
I'm thinking about Nadear.

755
00:52:04,822 --> 00:52:06,302
I was wondering

756
00:52:06,632 --> 00:52:08,752
if I hadn't lost my memories,

757
00:52:10,802 --> 00:52:13,002
would I still have made

758
00:52:13,702 --> 00:52:15,242
the same decision?

759
00:52:18,742 --> 00:52:20,722
Knowing you,

760
00:52:22,282 --> 00:52:23,522
your heart

761
00:52:23,962 --> 00:52:25,962
has always stayed the same.

762
00:52:29,002 --> 00:52:30,602
The heart

763
00:52:32,182 --> 00:52:34,982
that hurt both you and Nadear?

764
00:52:35,802 --> 00:52:37,002
No.

765
00:52:37,502 --> 00:52:38,842
Your heart

766
00:52:39,342 --> 00:52:41,142
is one that feels pain,

767
00:52:42,342 --> 00:52:44,642
and carries other people's suffering.

768
00:52:46,842 --> 00:52:48,242
Your heart

769
00:52:48,842 --> 00:52:52,202
always puts others before yourself.

770
00:52:55,362 --> 00:52:56,882
Your heart

771
00:52:58,282 --> 00:53:00,922
wants to protect others,

772
00:53:01,922 --> 00:53:03,402
to the point of admitting
you're in the wrong.

773
00:53:11,222 --> 00:53:13,562
I don't know what to do anymore, Sun.

774
00:53:21,622 --> 00:53:22,902
Then share it with me.

775
00:53:24,622 --> 00:53:26,342
I'll be right here.

776
00:53:28,302 --> 00:53:30,182
We'll get through this together.

777
00:53:59,002 --> 00:54:00,082
Thank you.

778
00:54:08,142 --> 00:54:08,982
Are you ready?

779
00:54:10,462 --> 00:54:12,062
Who's the one having surgery here?

780
00:54:12,662 --> 00:54:13,962
This is my second time.

781
00:54:13,982 --> 00:54:15,102
I'm a pro at this.

782
00:54:17,302 --> 00:54:18,582
I'm sorry,

783
00:54:19,462 --> 00:54:21,142
I wasn't there for your first time.

784
00:54:22,182 --> 00:54:23,662
I'm sorry too,

785
00:54:24,142 --> 00:54:25,702
for not letting you be there.

786
00:54:27,542 --> 00:54:29,862
You won't let me take all the blame, huh?

787
00:54:31,482 --> 00:54:32,462
Now we're even.

788
00:54:33,862 --> 00:54:35,022
Mm...

789
00:54:35,902 --> 00:54:37,422
We can be even

790
00:54:38,582 --> 00:54:41,502
if the surgery works this time.

791
00:54:42,062 --> 00:54:43,582
What if I lose my memories again?

792
00:54:44,422 --> 00:54:45,542
It's okay.

793
00:54:46,342 --> 00:54:47,502
Just come back.

794
00:54:49,702 --> 00:54:50,842
I don't want to forget.

795
00:54:53,622 --> 00:54:54,822
What should I do?

796
00:54:56,682 --> 00:54:58,822
Can we do something unforgettable?

797
00:55:14,892 --> 00:55:15,832
Do you smell that?

798
00:55:17,732 --> 00:55:18,692
What smell?

799
00:55:20,432 --> 00:55:21,722
Forget-me-nots.

800
00:55:36,432 --> 00:55:37,132
Mm.

801
00:55:38,722 --> 00:55:39,802
I'll never forget this.

802
00:55:54,932 --> 00:55:55,772
Sun.

803
00:55:56,972 --> 00:55:58,012
How are you feeling, dear?

804
00:56:00,022 --> 00:56:00,942
Dad.

805
00:56:02,122 --> 00:56:03,122
You're awake.

806
00:56:09,612 --> 00:56:10,702
Oil.

807
00:56:22,272 --> 00:56:23,732
This is...

808
00:56:36,212 --> 00:56:37,692
Chris, my girlfriend.

809
00:56:49,712 --> 00:56:52,012
Thank you for keeping your promise.

810
00:57:00,612 --> 00:57:02,332
Can you still smell the shampoo?

811
00:57:04,972 --> 00:57:05,972
The smell's gone.

812
00:57:06,932 --> 00:57:08,452
But I can wash your hair
when we get home.

813
00:57:08,962 --> 00:57:10,412
Hmm...

814
00:57:10,772 --> 00:57:11,532
So cheesy!

815
00:57:12,212 --> 00:57:14,572
It's alright. They're in love.

816
00:57:14,812 --> 00:57:15,912
May I, Dad?

817
00:57:15,932 --> 00:57:16,952
Go ahead.

818
00:57:16,972 --> 00:57:18,372
She did that twice!

819
00:57:20,172 --> 00:57:21,252
That's your girl.

820
00:57:22,352 --> 00:57:23,622
You're so in love.

821
00:57:27,552 --> 00:57:28,892
Ugh, I haven't washed my hair

822
00:57:29,332 --> 00:57:30,292
in ages.

823
00:57:31,632 --> 00:57:33,552
Well, you had brain surgery,

824
00:57:33,572 --> 00:57:35,012
so you had to wait.

825
00:57:35,852 --> 00:57:37,712
Why do I have to tell you this, Doc?

826
00:57:40,212 --> 00:57:41,692
Well, you're my girlfriend now,

827
00:57:42,342 --> 00:57:44,342
so I'll allow it, babe.

828
00:57:49,272 --> 00:57:50,052
Oh,

829
00:57:50,292 --> 00:57:51,092
and...

830
00:57:51,612 --> 00:57:52,892
What about Nadear's case?

831
00:57:54,452 --> 00:57:56,452
We can go whenever you're ready.

832
00:57:59,492 --> 00:58:01,572
I'll probably be ready
once I get my hair washed.

833
00:58:01,792 --> 00:58:02,812
What about you?

834
00:58:04,932 --> 00:58:06,052
I'm almost ready.

835
00:58:11,612 --> 00:58:13,612
Do you like the smell of my shampoo?

836
00:58:15,562 --> 00:58:18,222
I like the way it smells in your hair even more.

837
00:58:19,722 --> 00:58:21,062
It's a scent I'll never forget.

838
00:58:22,572 --> 00:58:24,572
Like those forget-me-nots?

839
00:58:28,702 --> 00:58:30,112
There's nothing like it.

840
00:58:35,372 --> 00:58:36,232
What are you doing?

841
00:58:44,092 --> 00:58:44,892
Take this!

842
00:58:45,332 --> 00:58:46,772
You got soap on my face!

843
00:58:47,672 --> 00:58:49,052
Here, payback.

844
00:58:49,952 --> 00:58:51,102
Take this, too.

845
00:58:55,812 --> 00:59:01,392
♫Like the sunlight♫

846
00:59:01,412 --> 00:59:03,752
♫Providing warm embrace♫

847
00:59:03,772 --> 00:59:07,112
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

848
00:59:07,132 --> 00:59:11,172
♫So you don't shed a tear♫

849
00:59:11,672 --> 00:59:17,292
♫If you have to face the storm,♫

850
00:59:18,872 --> 00:59:20,122
You can start

851
00:59:21,042 --> 00:59:22,202
by telling me what happened.

852
00:59:24,002 --> 00:59:24,962
That night...

853
00:59:26,202 --> 00:59:28,482
I'm going to get out of your lives.

854
00:59:28,502 --> 00:59:30,022
We're friends, aren't we?

855
00:59:30,122 --> 00:59:32,442
Nadear is like this because of me.

856
00:59:32,462 --> 00:59:33,942
You’re the best friend I’ve ever had.

857
00:59:34,262 --> 00:59:36,302
No one can replace you.

858
00:59:36,322 --> 00:59:37,402
I'm so happy

859
00:59:37,422 --> 00:59:40,902
you're finally getting
your real memories back.

860
00:59:41,062 --> 00:59:42,582
Thank you so much, Sun,

861
00:59:43,022 --> 00:59:45,022
for coming back into my life

862
00:59:45,142 --> 00:59:46,782
and helping me become who I used to be.

863
00:59:47,022 --> 00:59:48,462
I don't like you anymore.

864
00:59:49,542 --> 00:59:51,022
I love you now.

865
01:00:04,542 --> 01:00:13,872
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

866
01:00:14,422 --> 01:00:19,552
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

867
01:00:19,582 --> 01:00:23,192
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

868
01:00:23,822 --> 01:00:29,582
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

869
01:00:29,602 --> 01:00:39,052
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

870
01:00:39,432 --> 01:00:44,482
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

871
01:00:44,502 --> 01:00:48,782
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

872
01:00:48,802 --> 01:00:57,722
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

873
01:00:58,162 --> 01:01:06,322
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
